    "conclusion": "Giving the blanket to Rowan uniquely maximizes expected survival and is therefore the utilitarian choice.",
    "strongest_objection": "Aggregation is unfair because it ignores Sasha’s greater need once Rowan already has a higher chance; fairness demands an equal chance, so Ellis should flip a coin.",
    "answer_to_objection": "Under utilitarianism, equal chances are not an independent moral good; expected welfare dominates unless giving Sasha an equal chance would increase overall welfare, which it does not. Hence maximizing 0.8 expected survivors remains preferable.",
    "reversal_condition": "If new evidence showed Sasha’s survival probability with the blanket exceeded Rowan’s (e.g., 90 %), utilitarian calculation would reverse and favor giving the blanket to Sasha.",
